<title>JAPAN: Japan May lead imports dive 53.8 pct yr-on-yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May lead imports dive 53.8 pct yr-on-yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined lead imports in May dived 53.8 percent to 572 tonnes from 1,237 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data issued on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    May 97	  April 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Total	    572	     15,001	     1,237</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> China	    202		7,637		100</p>
<p> Australia	187		  189		 579</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first five months of 1997 were 19,843 tonnes, against 20,520 tonnes in the same period a year earlier. Lead imports usually surge in April due to the Generalised System of Preferences (GSP), which allows tariff exemptions for metal imports from designated developing countries.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
